{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_53","type":"agent_message","text":"# Review: SUGGESTIONS\n\n## Required Changes\n1. **Water-change profile validation**: the loop-2 partial-failure contract is only implemented for unknown profile IDs, not for invalid resolved profiles.\nCurrent: [`validate_water_changes`](/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/systems/water_change.rs#L5) only checks catalog membership, [`apply_water_change`](/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/systems/water_change.rs#L26) blindly applies the resolved profile, [`SourceWaterProfile`](/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/types/source_water.rs#L6) has no runtime validation, and [`check_non_negative`](/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/invariants.rs#L120) does not reject non-finite values. An invalid catalog entry from saved state or direct state construction can therefore partially mutate chemistry/temperature, or inject `NaN`, instead of failing atomically.\nExpected: validate the resolved `SourceWaterProfile` before any queued actions are applied, return a typed `SimError` for invalid runtime profiles, and leave `TankState`, queued actions, RNG state, clock, and event log unchanged on failure.\nReference: Loop-2 spec acceptance criterion, “Partial-failure invariant: if a queued water change references an unknown source profile or invalid resolved profile, `step_hours` returns a typed `SimError` and leaves state exactly unchanged.”\n\n## Recommended Improvements\n1. Scenario materialization should fail loudly on unsupported preset enum strings instead of silently defaulting to `InertSand`/`FastStem` in [`lib.rs`](/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_scenarios/src/lib.rs#L97) and [`lib.rs`](/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_scenarios/src/lib.rs#L122); that would match the typed-validation approach used elsewhere.\n2. I could not rerun `cargo test` in this environment because `cargo` is unavailable, so this review is based on source inspection and the checked-in tests."}}
